router ..> login
router ..> approval : URL → screen\n(linking config)
router ..> onb
splash ..> login
login ..> deviceMod : POST /v1/device/code\n(on page load)
approval ..> deviceMod : GET /v1/device/pending\nPOST /v1/device/approve
profilScreen ..> authMod : device list · revoke
login ..> authClient
login ..> apiclient : useAuthCapabilities…\n(is Google actually configured?)
onb ..> apiclient
cockpitScreen ..> apiclient : useCockpit…GetCockpitSummary
cockpitScreen ..> core : formatEuroRange()
profilScreen ..> apiclient : useProfile…Get / Put
profilScreen ..> core : isValidSteuerId()
datenschutzScreen ..> apiclient : useAccountDeletion…DeleteAccount
datenschutzScreen ..> authClient : useSession()\nguest vs. account
datenschutzScreen ..> exportDl : runExport(json | pdf)
fe --> ui
ui ..> tokens

authClient ..> betterauth : HTTP  /api/auth/*  (credentialed)
apiclient ..> api : HTTP  /v1/*  (cookie-scoped)
exportDl ..> api : HTTP  GET /v1/account/export\n(credentialed, binary attachment)

deviceMod ..> betterauth : auth.api.deviceCode/Verify/\nApprove/Token — server-side only,\nthe plugin's HTTP routes are off
deviceMod ..> region : resolve(ip) → country | "unknown"
deviceMod --> prisma

betterauth --> prisma
guard ..> betterauth : resolves the session
guard --> profile
guard --> cockpitMod
guard --> accountMod
authMod --> betterauth
profile --> prisma
profile --> audit
cockpitMod ..> core : cockpitRange()\n(determinism boundary,\nADR-014/048)
cockpitMod --> prisma
accountMod ..> profile : reuses ProfileRepository\n(one decrypt path)
accountMod --> audit
accountMod ..> authMod : FreshAuthChecker\n(fresh session or password)
accountMod --> prisma
audit --> prisma
prisma --> db
crosscut ..> api

note bottom of exportDl
  The **one** sanctioned exception to "all /v1 traffic goes through
  @steuereule/api-client's httpClient mutator" (ADR-0001): the export
  is a `Content-Disposition: attachment` body — JSON *or* PDF bytes —
  and the mutator unconditionally JSON.parse()s. It reuses the same
  configured origin and the same `credentials: 'include'` discipline,
  and it is drawn here rather than hidden inside the screen precisely
  because an undrawn second egress is how "one call site" quietly
  stops being true.
end note

note right of deviceMod
  **ADR-0024 — the plugin runs behind our endpoints.**
  It is never in front of the browser: better-auth's device-authorization routes are
  switched off via `disabledPaths`; only `auth.api.*` server-side
  calls reach it. Two findings force this: `/device/token` returns a
  Bearer token in JSON and never sets a cookie (ADR-0008/0012 forbid
  holding one in JS-reachable storage), and `/device` (GET) claims a
  code for the caller's account while the origin check skips all GETs
  — reachable cross-site under our `SameSite=None` cookie.
  Same shape as the UserContextGuard seam: better-auth is the
  mechanism, our API owns the surface.
end note

note bottom of router
  **ADR-0023 — the router lives here and only here.** Screens stay
  prop-driven: a screen never imports `@react-navigation/*`, never
  calls a navigation hook, never imports a navigation type. That
  constraint is what keeps the 14 prop-mounted test files untouched
  (blast radius 1, not 15) — and it is enforced at review, not hoped for.
end note

note right of accountMod
  Deletion is **one Prisma $transaction** (ADR-0013 §3):
  hard-delete Profile · anonymise the audit rows to an
  irreversible tombstone (the Art. 30 record survives, the
  person-link does not) · delete the better-auth User
  (Session/Account cascade). Rows under an active LegalHold
  are exempt. All-or-nothing, never a partial teardown.
end note

legend right
  All /v1 access is scoped by the trusted userId the UserContextGuard
  establishes (ADR-0007/0012) — a verified better-auth session or an
  HMAC-signed guest cookie, never a client-supplied identity.
  better-auth (ADR-0009) mounts *behind* that seam, not around it.
  @steuereule/core is the single home of deterministic rules
  (validators, cockpitRange), imported by both api and frontend.
endlegend

@enduml
